hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20913","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say, and Yazid ibn Harun, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Aidh ibn Amr entered, Yazid said: And he was among the righteous companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The worst shepherds are the cruel. Abd al-Rahman said: I think he said: Beware of being among them, and Yazid did not doubt, so he said: Sit, you are only from the bran of the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And was there bran among them or in them, bran was only after them and in others than them."
"20914","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Shimr al-Dubai who said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr forbidding dubba and hantam and muzaffat and naqir, so I said to him: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes."
"20915","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from a shaykh in the gathering of Abu Uthman from Aidh ibn Amr who said: Water was scarce, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution in a cup or in a bowl, and he sprinkled us with it. He said: And the fortunate among us was he who got some of it, and we do not think but that it reached all the people. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us the forenoon prayer."
"20916","Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid Abu Shibl and Hasan, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us with the meaning from Thabit from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from Aidh ibn Amr that Salman and Suhayb and Bilal were sitting among people, and Abu Sufyan ibn Harb passed by them, and they said: The swords of Allah, blessed and exalted, have not yet taken their due from the neck of the enemy of Allah. Abu Bakr said: Do you say this to the elder of Quraysh and its chief. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was informed of that, so he said: O Abu Bakr, perhaps you angered them, for if you angered them you have angered your Lord, blessed and exalted. So he returned to them and said: O our brothers, perhaps you are angry. They said: No, O Abu Bakr, may Allah forgive you."
"20917","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us the like with its chain."
"20918","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal, a shaykh of his, narrated to us from Aidh ibn Amr who said: I think he raised it, he said: Whoever gets some of this provision, let him expand his provision with it, and if he is independent of it, let him direct it to one more needy of it than him."
"20919","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from Aidh ibn Amr that Suhayb and Salman and Bilal were sitting, then he mentioned the like, except that he said: So he went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of that, so he said: O Abu Bakr."
"20920","Rawh narrated to us, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalifah ibn Abdullah al-Ghubari say: I heard Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani say: While we were with our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the hadith of begging."
"20921","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah who said: I heard Abu Shimr al-Dubai, he said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: I said to Yahya ibn Said: Al-Muzani. He said: Yes. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hantam and dubba and naqir and muzaffat."
"20922","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalifah ibn Abdullah al-Ghubari say: I heard Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani say: While we were with our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a Bedouin insisted upon him in begging, saying: O Messenger of Allah, feed me, O Messenger of Allah, give me. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and entered the house and took hold of the two doorposts of the chamber and turned to us with his face and said: By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you knew what I know about begging, no man would ask another man while having a night that shelters him. So he ordered food for him."
"20923","Yunus and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, Abd al-Samad said: A shaykh of his, from Aidh ibn Amr from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said, Abd al-Samad said: I think he raised it, he said: Whoever gets some of this provision, and Yunus said: Without asking nor aspiring, let him expand his provision with it, and if he is independent of it, let him direct it to one more needy of it than him."
"20924","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us from Amir al-Ahwal who said: Aidh ibn Amr said from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever gets some of this provision without asking nor aspiring, let him expand his provision with it, and if he is independent of it, let him direct it to one more needy of it than him."
"20925","Waki narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us from Amir al-Ahwal from Aidh ibn Amr who said, Abu al-Ashhab said: I think he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whomever Allah, blessed and exalted, gives provision without asking, let him accept it. Abdullah said: I asked my father: What is aspiring. He said: You say to yourself: So-and-so will send to me, so-and-so will join me."
